join Lindi (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
Lindi: 'Second outbreak, reduced density, processing complete within forty-eight hours of collection.'
Lindi: That's not how you talk to yourself in a field.
- It sounded fine to me
	Hope: It sounded fine to me.
	Lindi: It sounded like a lab notebook.
	Lindi: I did one semester. Environmental science, at the university. One.
	- Ask what happened
		Hope: What happened?
		Lindi: I couldn't pay for the second one.
		Lindi: So I came home.
	- I didn't know that
		Hope: I didn't know that.
		Lindi: Ledi knows. Mama Zulu knows. It's not a secret, it's just not a thing I bring up.
Lindi: I've kept doing it anyway. Four years of surveys nobody asked for, in a format nobody's going to read, because I liked the format.
Lindi: It's the only way I know how to look at anything properly, I write it down and then I can see the —
Lindi: Is that silly? Keeping it up like that. For nothing.
- It's not for nothing. Charity uses your water data.
	Hope: It's not for nothing. Charity uses your water data.
	Lindi: She uses three numbers out of about four hundred pages.
	Lindi: That's not a complaint. It's just — you asked, and that's the honest size of it.
- No. It's not silly.
	Hope: No. It's not silly.
	Lindi: ...All right.
Lindi: I don't know why I asked. I know it isn't.
Lindi: I think I wanted somebody to have heard me say the word 'semester' out loud. That's all.
Lindi: Right. There's a rack that needs turning.
[signal arg="hearts:lindi:2"]
set {GameState.quest_lindi_correspondence_course} = "complete"
